WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.760
so I really went back and forth about whether
to even do this story today about how

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.810
still is no connection between undocumented
immigrants and criminality.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.170
Because on the one hand we've already covered
this story.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:17.800
It's sort of obvious that this is the case,
but there are still so many people who believe

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.740
deeply believe that undocumented immigrants
are more likely to commit crimes in the United

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.740
States.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.850
So ultimately I made the case that it is worth
debunking once again.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.981
And before I even tell you about the new report,
let's just remind ourselves of some of the

00:00:29.981 --> 00:00:33.219
obvious realities coming to the United States.

00:00:33.219 --> 00:00:35.039
Illegally is illegal.

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:39.800
Uh, it can be a misdemeanor or a civil infraction
depending on whether you've overstayed a visa

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.109
or a crossing the border without permission.

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:43.679
That's not what's at issue here.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:44.679
Okay?

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:49.789
What does that issue here is whether undocumented
immigrants do or do not commit more crime

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:55.069
than native born Americans or more crime than
legal immigrants to the United States.

00:00:55.069 --> 00:00:58.940
And we hear a lot of specific anecdotes from
Donald Trump and and right wingers who have

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.649
propagandized around this, about crimes committed
by undocumented immigrants.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:09.550
And of course in a country this big, there
are examples of everything, but this is important

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:16.870
because our policy towards immigration would
be different depending on whether or not undocumented

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:22.560
immigrants actually are more likely to commit
violent crime and property crime in the United

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.560
States.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.130
But this is pretty obvious.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.450
Undocumented immigrants know that they are
undocumented.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.640
They know that if they get into trouble with
the authorities, if they come to the attention

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.090
of law enforcement, not only it could they
suffer the penalties for the crime that they

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.340
commit, but they could be deported.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.570
They could get in trouble for being undocumented.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:50.210
So why would a group that knows they have
an extra incentive to stay off the radar of

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.650
law enforcement?

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:57.380
Why would they commit crimes at a higher rate
than native born Americans and legal immigrants

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.850
and attract the attention of law enforcement?

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:03.310
Yes, we know that poverty and crime are connected.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.659
Many undocumented immigrants are poor, but
the research has shown for a long time that

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:10.969
undocumented immigrants aren't more likely
to be violent criminals.

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:14.560
And yet again, we have a new study with pew
data.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.690
Pew Research Center data analyzed by the Marshall
Project with tells us that undocumented immigrants

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:26.489
don't increase crime rates, whether or not
undocumented immigration to a metro area increased.

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:31.700
The crime rates have continued to slowly decline
more or less equally.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:37.379
And in fact, there are many areas with more
undocumented immigration that have had even

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:44.040
larger decreases in crime even though it's
by a small amount and maybe not statistically

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.049
significant.

00:02:45.049 --> 00:02:49.470
Now this is not to argue that we shouldn't
deal with undocumented immigration, which

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.920
is still a crime, right?

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.730
Although it's only a civil infraction or a
misdemeanor.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.189
Again, depending on whether you're talking
about an overstayed a visa or crossing the

00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:03.180
border without permission, but we cannot allow
this discussion to be framed as we have a

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:08.049
crisis of violent undocumented immigrants
in the United States because we don't, and

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:13.909
this is actually the epitome of how the Republican
Party often very successfully influences public

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:15.060
opinion.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:22.999
The principal is they take an anecdote and
they exploited to make people scared or angry

00:03:22.999 --> 00:03:26.079
and to eventually support bad policy policy.

00:03:26.079 --> 00:03:27.480
That doesn't actually make sense.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.959
So let me do an analogy.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:31.950
A first to abortion.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.499
They come out, they say extreme late term
abortions have to be stopped.

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:38.430
Democrats are killing babies.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.430
This is horrible.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:44.450
When you look at it, you realize, wait a second,
extreme late term abortion is really rare.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:49.889
And when it's something that takes place,
the baby often is going to die anyway within

00:03:49.889 --> 00:03:55.169
days or weeks of, of coming out of the uterus.

00:03:55.169 --> 00:03:58.750
And it more becomes a question of the life
of the mother.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.949
It becomes a question of how soon is this
fetus going to be determined?

00:04:03.949 --> 00:04:05.189
Non-Viable.

00:04:05.189 --> 00:04:10.599
But Republicans use the straw man of the post
birth abortion and all of these crazy things

00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:13.420
to justify trying to ban abortion altogether.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.510
This is the same thing going on with, uh,
with undocumented immigration.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:20.150
An illegal as they like to say, killed this
person.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.990
Well, that's a crime.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.220
It's a tragedy.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.220
It's horrifying.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.220
Okay.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.870
I would not even think of minimizing the horrible
nature of that.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:33.910
But the real discussion around undocumented
immigration is, is not actually about crime.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.460
It's about economics.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.270
It's about culture, it's about geopolitics.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.590
It's about diplomacy and foreign relations
and foreign policy.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.720
That's the real conversation around undocumented
immigration.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.230
And the problem is that if you actually have
the conversation on those terms instead of

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:57.540
about these crimes that Donald Trump and others
like to point to, um, the, the outcome, the

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.230
right path forward becomes one that the American
right simply doesn't want.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:08.490
It becomes one of working to minimize the,
uh, circumstances in the source countries

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:12.380
of undocumented immigration that make people
want to come here to begin with.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:17.510
It becomes an issue of dealing with the economic
conditions and the large corporations that

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:23.370
are actually a big driver for that undocumented
immigration because they are employing undocumented

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.370
immigrants.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.750
If you actually deal with undocumented immigration
as an economic, cultural and geopolitical

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:34.590
issue, you can't justify the policies that
Republicans want, which is why they have to

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:39.450
couch it in these terms of dangerous brown
people coming over the border.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.490
Yet another study tells us it's absolutely
ridiculous.

